00:20:24,528 --> 00:20:26,553
它把子弹碎片或门框碎屑撞得四散……
It knocked bits of bullet
or bits of doorframe...

311
00:20:26,588 --> 00:20:30,489
于是子弹碎了，……变成了更多子弹。
So the bullet shatters and...
.. turns into more bullets.

312
00:20:30,524 --> 00:20:34,540
是啊，兄弟，你在里面应该没事，别管它。
Yeah. You're going to be all right
in there, mate. Nothing to see here.

313
00:20:36,544 --> 00:20:39,497
离伊朗边境还有30英里，
With 30 miles to go
to the Iranian border,

314
00:20:39,532 --> 00:20:43,556
詹姆斯用一段小圣诞颂歌镇定了神经。
James calmed his nerves
with a little carol concert.

315
00:20:43,591 --> 00:20:46,533
♪ 我们三个BBC二台的伙计
♪ We three blokes from BBC Two

316
00:20:46,568 --> 00:20:49,509
♪ 一辆金色车，一辆屎黄色车，
♪ One colour gold
car, one colour poo,

317
00:20:49,544 --> 00:20:52,568
♪ 哦哦，带错了车，也带对了，
♪ Oh-oh, brought the wrong
cars, brought the right,

318
00:20:52,603 --> 00:20:55,553
♪ 暖气正常，灯也亮，
♪ Working heater, working lights,

319
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:59,536
♪ 向西的垫圈可能要爆炸
♪ Westward-going
Gasket maybe blowing

320
00:20:59,571 --> 00:21:00,572
♪ 真是个烂玩意…
♪ What a piece of sh...

321
00:21:09,504 --> 00:21:11,465
我猜前面那座城镇
I believe that town ahead of us

322
00:21:11,500 --> 00:21:14,580
是边境前的最后一座城镇。没错！
is the last townbefore
the border. Yes!

323
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:24,545
抱歉。
Sorry.

324
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:28,556
好了，伙计们。把文书弄好。
This is it, chaps.
Sort out the paperwork.

325
00:21:28,591 --> 00:21:30,585
马上见。
See you in a sec.

326
00:21:30,620 --> 00:21:32,545
这可真是松了口气。
That's a relief.

327
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:35,580
我的大灯不给力。  
不对，我这边也不行。
My headlights aren't very good.
No, mine aren't.

328
00:21:39,512 --> 00:21:41,564
杰里米回得相当快。
'Jeremy was back rather quickly. '

329
00:21:42,536 --> 00:21:45,580
好吧，坏消息。
Right. Bad news.

330
00:21:45,615 --> 00:21:47,504
什么？
What?

331
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:52,524
因政治因素，BBC不准进伊朗。
For political reasons, the
BBC is not allowed into Iran.

332
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:55,557
不给进？你说什么？BBC里没人……
Not allowed? You what?
No-one from the BBC...

333
00:21:55,592 --> 00:21:59,070
我以为只有BBC新闻被禁，结果是整个BBC
I thought it was just BBC
News, but the whole BBC

334
00:21:59,105 --> 00:22:02,548
都进不了伊朗，所以我们过不了边境。
is not allowed in Iran so
we can't cross the border.

335
00:22:02,583 --> 00:22:04,497
连汽车节目都进不了吗...？
A car show isn't allowed into...?

336
00:22:04,532 --> 00:22:08,504
算了……别纠结了。我们根本进不了。
Never mind... Let's not get bogged down.
We aren't allowed in.

337
00:22:08,539 --> 00:22:10,481
那安迪和迪克能来吗？
So Ant and Dec can come here?

338
00:22:10,516 --> 00:22:15,556
安迪和迪克、西蒙·考尔、克里斯·塔朗特……《第五汽轮》？
Ant and Dec, Simon Cowell,C
hris Tarrant... Fifth Gear?

339
00:22:15,591 --> 00:22:17,513
《第五汽轮》。埃默代尔农场？
Fifth Gear. Emmerdale Farm?

340
00:22:17,548 --> 00:22:20,592
埃默代尔农场但没有大卫·阿滕伯勒，也没我们。春季观察？
Emmerdale Farm but not
DavidAttenborough, not us. Springwatch?

341
00:22:22,540 --> 00:22:26,504
我们查了地图，形势相当惨淡。
'We consulted the map and
the situation was bleak.

342
00:22:26,539 --> 00:22:27,557
东边已经没有路了。
'East was now out.

343
00:22:27,592 --> 00:22:29,521
巴格达在南边
'Baghdad was to the south

344
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:33,064
而伊斯兰圣战组织的大本营摩苏尔在西面。
'and the Al-Qaeda stronghold
of Mosul was to the west.

345
00:22:33,099 --> 00:22:36,572
我们唯一的选择是下山走那条山路
'Our only option was to go
back down the mountain road

346
00:22:36,607 --> 00:22:41,525
然后试图找条安全的路北上去土耳其。
'and try and find a safe
road north into Turkey. '

347
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:44,596
我打赌那三位智者从没遇到过这种事。
I bet the original three wise
men never had this problem.

348
00:22:44,631 --> 00:22:48,485
哎呀，他们又不是BBC。
Well, they weren't BBC, were they?

349
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:52,544
我们觉得夜里走山路太冒险，
We thought it too risky to tackle
the mountain road at night,

350
00:22:52,579 --> 00:22:56,081
于是只能找地方落脚。
so now we had to find
somewhere to stay.

351
00:22:56,116 --> 00:22:59,549
根本没有哪儿像旅店。
There is nothing even
remotely hotelish.

352
00:22:59,584 --> 00:23:02,560
我们在夜里行驶，  
根本没有落脚的地方。
We're travelling at night,
we have nowhere to stay.

353
00:23:03,592 --> 00:23:06,580
大概是我们现在能干的最糟糕的事。
Probably the worst thing
we could do right now.

354
00:23:08,536 --> 00:23:09,596
前面有灯光，伙计们。
Lights ahead, chaps.

355
00:23:19,568 --> 00:23:21,561
第二天早晨，结果
The following
morning, it turned out

356
00:23:21,596 --> 00:23:25,524
我们居然住进了伊拉克的一个游乐园，挺奇怪的。
we'd stayed at an Iraqi amusement
park, which was a bit weird.

357
00:23:34,552 --> 00:23:36,592
那是理查德·哈蒙德。
That's Richard Hammond.

358
00:23:44,552 --> 00:23:48,493
我们坐在游乐设施上时，突然意识到点什么。
While we were on the rides,
we realised something.

359
00:23:48,528 --> 00:23:51,564
我们在伊拉克已经两天了，  
却一次也没被打中，
We'd been in Iraq for two days and
we hadn't been shot even once,

360
00:23:51,599 --> 00:23:54,580
也没被炸掉，甚至没在网络上被砍头。
or blown up or beheaded
on the internet.

361
00:23:54,615 --> 00:23:58,528
简而言之，我们灵机一动。
In short, we had an epiphany.

362
00:24:01,548 --> 00:24:03,473
我可不想再穿这玩意儿了。
I'm not wearing this any more.

363
00:24:03,508 --> 00:24:06,536
我很高兴你这么说，我根本就不需要这个。
I'm glad you said that.
I haven't felt in need of this.

364
00:24:06,571 --> 00:24:08,501
啊……
Ahhh...

365
00:24:08,536 --> 00:24:11,485
我真高兴我们没去伊朗，
I'm glad we're not going to Iran,

366
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:13,521
因为，抱歉，我知道这里是伊拉克，好吧，
cos I'm sorry, I know
this is Iraq, OK,

367
00:24:13,556 --> 00:24:18,528
但这里是伊拉克的库尔德斯坦地区，满是库尔德人。
but it's the Kurdistan region
of Iraq so it's full of Kurds.

368
00:24:18,563 --> 00:24:20,525
他们都挺可爱的。
They're all lovely.

369
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:24,553
大家都超友好，危险程度跟切尔滕纳姆差不多。
Everybody's very friendly.
It's about as dangerous as Cheltenham.

370
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:29,520
来吧，阳光正好，三辆敞篷跑车，我们在山里。
So come on, the sun is out, three
convertible sports cars, we're in the
mountains.

371
00:24:29,555 --> 00:24:31,576
我们可以再走一遍同样的路，不过好好享受一下。
We can go down the same
road again, but enjoy it.

372
00:24:41,516 --> 00:24:43,517
哇！照常营业啊。
Wow! Business as usual.

373
00:24:43,552 --> 00:24:47,504
这简直不可思议，我正开着马自达MX-5，
This is incredible.
I'm in a Mazda MX-5,

374
00:24:47,539 --> 00:24:49,544
在伊拉克里飞驰。
plunging through Iraq.

375
00:24:49,579 --> 00:24:51,556
啊哈——！
Ah ha-ha!

376
00:24:53,556 --> 00:24:56,516
恐惧消散后，我们终于可以
With the fear gone, we
could for the first time

377
00:24:56,551 --> 00:24:58,580
开始思考我们买的车了。
think about the cars we'd bought.

378
00:25:02,536 --> 00:25:05,576
来吧，小Barchetta，咱们看看你有几把刷子。
Come on then, little Barchetta,
let's see what you've got.

379
00:25:06,568 --> 00:25:09,537
奇怪的是，这三辆里，
The weird thing is, of the three,

380
00:25:09,572 --> 00:25:12,545
这台最不像传统敞篷车。
this is the least like
a traditional roadster.

381
00:25:12,580 --> 00:25:16,572
它是前轮驱动，底子是菲亚特Punto的。
It's front-wheel-drive, it's
based on a Fiat Punto underneath.

382
00:25:16,607 --> 00:25:19,481
但它是辆极具光彩的小车。
But this is a glorious little car.

383
00:25:19,516 --> 00:25:22,524
前轮驱动的事根本不重要。
The whole front wheel-drive
issue just doesn't matter.

384
00:25:22,559 --> 00:25:26,516
这车的感觉很特别，这就足够了
This feels special and
that's all that matters

385
00:25:26,551 --> 00:25:27,560
在两座敞篷车里。
in a two-seater roadster.

386
00:25:31,504 --> 00:25:33,513
说到MX-5，你们也懂的，
As you'd expect with an MX-5,

387
00:25:33,548 --> 00:25:37,552
它身上的每个细节都是完美的。
every single thing
on it is perfect.

388
00:25:39,564 --> 00:25:41,572
除了这扇门上几个洞。
Apart from some holes in this door.

389
00:25:42,572 --> 00:25:45,560
子弹怎么会在马自达里分成三块
How does a bullet
split into three parts

390
00:25:45,595 --> 00:25:47,596
在车里穿行时？
while travelling through a Mazda?

391
00:25:47,631 --> 00:25:50,525
我觉得这是个暗示。
I think it's a sign.

392
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:54,516
父亲、儿子，还有那扇神圣之门。
The Father, the Son
and the Holy Door.

393
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:59,497
与此同时，后座……
Meanwhile, at the back...

394
00:25:59,532 --> 00:26:03,524
观众们，咱俩私下里说，我可能搞错点儿了。
Viewers, strictly between you and me,
I may have made a bit of an error.

395
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:05,521
呃……
Erm...

396
00:26:05,556 --> 00:26:06,549
我该怎么说呢？
How can I put it?

397
00:26:06,584 --> 00:26:10,064
发动机太小，悬挂太软，
The engine is too small,
the suspension is too soft

398
00:26:10,099 --> 00:26:13,544
而且档位间的间隙大得离谱，
and the gaps between the
gear ratios are so big,

399
00:26:13,579 --> 00:26:16,500
我都能在里头装个别的变速箱。
I could get another
gearbox in them.

400
00:26:16,535 --> 00:26:19,596
来吧！换档吧。
Come on! And change.

401
00:26:22,516 --> 00:26:23,524
谢谢。
Thank you.

402
00:26:30,584 --> 00:26:34,046
当我们深入伊拉克北部时，
As we headed deeper
into northern Iraq,

403
00:26:34,081 --> 00:26:37,473
风景变得更加壮观。
the scenery became
even more spectacular.

404
00:26:37,508 --> 00:26:41,532
说实话，我从未去过比这里更美的地方。
I can honestly say I don't think I've
ever been anywhere more beautiful.

405
00:26:41,567 --> 00:26:43,548
真是令人动容的美。
It's movingly beautiful.

406
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:51,545
我真是太高兴了
I am so glad

407
00:26:51,580 --> 00:26:55,540
我们没被允许进伊朗，要是我们现在在那儿，
we weren't allowed into Iran
cos if we were there now,

408
00:26:55,575 --> 00:26:58,532
我根本看不到这片令人惊叹的景色。
I wouldn't be seeing
this incredible place.

409
00:26:58,567 --> 00:27:01,512
我们当初为何在这里害怕呢？
Why were we ever frightened here?

410
00:27:04,568 --> 00:27:07,505
可惜，并不是整个伊拉克都这么安宁，
Sadly, not all of
Iraq is this peaceful,

411
00:27:07,540 --> 00:27:11,536
于是第二天早晨我们找到了通往土耳他的路，出发了，
so the next morning we found
a road to Turkey and set off,

412
00:27:11,571 --> 00:27:14,520
仍然远离伯利恒。
still heading away from Bethlehem.

413
00:27:19,576 --> 00:27:22,505
杰里米头上戴着个碟子一样的玩意儿，
Jeremy's got a dish-dash
thing on his head

414
00:27:22,540 --> 00:27:26,040
看起来像个‘无能的劳伦斯’，
which makes him look like
Lawrence of Incompetence.

415
00:27:26,075 --> 00:27:29,540
不过好歹他学会了几句当地话，
But at least he had managed
to learn a few local words,

416
00:27:29,575 --> 00:27:33,548
在下一个加油站派上了用场。
which came in handy at
the next filling station.

417
00:27:33,583 --> 00:27:35,529
记住，
Just remember,

418
00:27:35,564 --> 00:27:37,532
“bhedji”是汽油。
"bhedji" is petrol.

419
00:27:38,524 --> 00:27:39,541
“Bhedji”是混蛋。
"Bhedji" is bastard.

420
00:27:39,576 --> 00:27:42,504
所以，无论如何别弄错了。
So don't, whatever you
do, get that wrong.

421
00:27:42,539 --> 00:27:43,584
这里有人吗？
Is there anybody here?

422
00:27:45,540 --> 00:27:47,520
‘有……算是有吧。’
'There was... sort of. '

423
00:27:54,572 --> 00:27:57,552
我不想为了点汽油把人叫醒。
I don't like to wake a man
up just for some petrol.

424
00:27:57,587 --> 00:28:00,532
尤其是我不小心叫他‘混蛋’的时候。
Especially if I accidentally
call him a bastard.

425
00:28:03,540 --> 00:28:08,592
于是我们一路跋涉，很快抵达了那让人害怕的土耳其边境。
So we trundled onwards and soon we
arrived at the scary Turkish border.

426
00:28:13,508 --> 00:28:17,568
哎……这儿怎么看都不太友好。
Oh... This doesn't feel
friendly at all somehow.

427
00:28:20,592 --> 00:28:23,504
下车？好啊，拜托。好的。
Out the car? Yes, please. OK.

428
00:28:34,516 --> 00:28:36,584
他要干什么？
What's he going to do?

429
00:28:47,500 --> 00:28:48,592
那是罐装的……
That's a can of...

430
00:28:48,627 --> 00:28:50,489
哦……
Oh...

431
00:28:50,524 --> 00:28:53,473
这是什么？我来解释。
What is this? I can explain.

432
00:28:53,508 --> 00:28:55,552
这…这呃…是个打火机。
It's... It's erm... it's a lighter.

433
00:28:55,587 --> 00:28:59,512
打火机？对。不好意思。
Lighter? Yeah. Sorry.

434
00:28:59,547 --> 00:29:01,465
你确定吗？
Are you sure?

435
00:29:01,500 --> 00:29:02,576
是啊。给你看…看到没？
Yeah. Can I show it to you... See?

436
00:29:02,611 --> 00:29:05,541
它呃…如果你这么做。
It erm... If you do that.

437
00:29:05,576 --> 00:29:07,588
然后它…哦，根本不工作。
Then it... Oh, it doesn't work.

438
00:29:07,623 --> 00:29:09,605
你真有趣。
You are a funny man.

439
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:11,588
是啊。抱歉。抱歉。
Yeah. Sorry. Sorry.

440
00:29:14,536 --> 00:29:16,572
好吧，我想我刚刚喝了点小酒。
OK, I think I may
have just had a wee.

441
00:29:17,584 --> 00:29:23,532
在边境的另一侧，
我们停下来接受新指示。
On the other side of the border, we
pulled over for new instructions.

442
00:29:24,584 --> 00:29:27,504
他们已经进来了。可预料的。
They've moved in. Predictable.

443
00:29:28,568 --> 00:29:30,538
你们这些白痴。
You idiots.

444
00:29:30,573 --> 00:29:32,473
是的。强劲。
Yes. Strong.

445
00:29:32,508 --> 00:29:37,592
你们已经逃离了没有战争的地区，
现在进入了有战乱的地方。
You have escaped from a region where there
is no war into a region where there is.

446
00:29:39,556 --> 00:29:42,572
库尔德人正在为独立而与
土耳其人作战，
The Kurds are fighting the
Turks for independence,

447
00:29:42,607 --> 00:29:45,537
所以如果你们真的是聪明人，
so if you really are wise men,

448
00:29:45,572 --> 00:29:49,548
你们会在天黑之前到达
安全区的酒店。
you will get to your hotel in
the safe zone by nightfall.

449
00:29:52,556 --> 00:29:54,465
还有更多……
And more...

450
00:29:54,500 --> 00:29:56,541
啊，外交部。
Ah, Foreign Office.

451
00:29:56,576 --> 00:30:00,465
英国政府外交部旅行概况。
British Government Foreign
Office travel summary.

452
00:30:00,500 --> 00:30:04,536
我们建议除必要外，避免前往
哈卡里、锡尔纳克、希尔特和通杰利省。
We advise against all but essential
travel in the provinces of Hakkari,

453
00:30:04,571 --> 00:30:07,524
锡尔纳克、希尔特和通杰利省。
Sirnak, Siirt and Tunceli.

454
00:30:11,508 --> 00:30:13,572
截至今年已发生九起袭击。
Nine attacks this year so far.

455
00:30:13,607 --> 00:30:15,516
恐怖主义威胁极高。
High threat of terrorism.

456
00:30:16,580 --> 00:30:18,505
这比伊拉克还糟。
This is worse then, than Iraq.

457
00:30:18,540 --> 00:30:21,528
我以为我已经和这事说再见了。
I thought I'd said goodbye to this.

458
00:30:21,563 --> 00:30:23,520
那就是我们要去的地方吗？
Is that where we're going?

459
00:30:23,555 --> 00:30:25,533
我们要去…
We're going to...

460
00:30:25,568 --> 00:30:27,477
那是 220 英里。
That's 220 miles.

461
00:30:27,512 --> 00:30:29,544
相当于 363 公里。
That's 363 kilometres.

462
00:30:29,579 --> 00:30:32,469
那是 220 英里。
That's 220 miles.

463
00:30:32,504 --> 00:30:36,529
我们还有 220 英里要跑…
We've got 220 miles to do in...

464
00:30:36,564 --> 00:30:39,580
四个半小时。
四个半小时。不可能啊。
Four and a half hours.
Fourand a half hours. Not possible.

465
00:30:43,584 --> 00:30:47,532
抱歉，伙计们，这已经变成了一场
谁的车最快的测试
I'm afraid, chaps, this
has just become a test

466
00:30:47,567 --> 00:30:49,572
谁的车最快。
of who's got the fastest car.

467
00:30:52,508 --> 00:30:53,516
