1080
01:08:16,512 --> 01:08:20,564
至于刺伤他手臂的刺……没有证据。
And the thorn what hath pricked
his arm... No evidence.

1081
01:08:20,599 --> 01:08:22,541
它自己都搞砸了……
It got better of its own...

1082
01:08:22,576 --> 01:08:25,500
这就是会发生的事！  
那是几天前的事！
That's what happens!
It was days ago!

1083
01:08:26,504 --> 01:08:27,517
倒抽气
GASPS

1084
01:08:27,552 --> 01:08:30,560
我这袋子里原本只有一颗糖，现在却全变成一堆了。
I only had one sweet in this
bag and now there are many.

1085
01:08:30,595 --> 01:08:33,500
不，是一袋子糖啊。
No, it was a bag full of sweets.

1086
01:08:38,512 --> 01:08:41,032
第二天早上，在加利利的湖畔，
The next morning, on
the shores of Galilee,

1087
01:08:41,067 --> 01:08:43,517
我们稍微安静地沉思了一下。
we had a moment of
quiet contemplation.

1088
01:08:43,552 --> 01:08:48,524
…我们还有足够的剩饭，足够装满12个篮子。
".. we still had enough food
left over to fill 12 baskets. "

1089
01:08:48,559 --> 01:08:51,516
于是，仍然沉浸在幻想中的杰里米
And then, the
still-delusional Jeremy

1090
01:08:51,551 --> 01:08:53,528
又提议再做一次饭菜。
offered to cook yet another meal.

1091
01:08:53,563 --> 01:08:55,521
只有两条鱼。
There's only two fish.

1092
01:08:55,556 --> 01:08:58,548
我不喜欢吃鱼。好吧，给你，我已经想好了。
I don't like fish. Well, there
you are, I've solved it.

1093
01:08:58,583 --> 01:09:01,516
这是个奇迹。那真是奇迹。简直不敢相信！
It's a miracle.
That is a miracle. Hardly!

1094
01:09:01,551 --> 01:09:03,520
鱼够大家分的。
We've got enough fish to go round.

1095
01:09:05,588 --> 01:09:08,044
我现在在水面上行走。
I am walking on water now.

1096
01:09:08,079 --> 01:09:09,817
你站在上面呀。
You're standing on it.

1097
01:09:09,852 --> 01:09:11,556
往那边走。行。
Walk over there. Yeah.

1098
01:09:15,596 --> 01:09:19,536
真是神迹啊，兄弟。我发明了游泳！天啊。
Miraculous that, mate.
I've invented swimming! Oh, God.

1099
01:09:19,571 --> 01:09:21,485
你觉得怎么样？
What do you think of that?

1100
01:09:21,520 --> 01:09:26,508
‘在杰里米决定分开水面之前，我们已经继续前进了。’
'Before Jeremy decided to part
the waters, we moved on. '

1101
01:09:28,568 --> 01:09:31,054
我感觉糟透了。
I feel awful.

1102
01:09:31,089 --> 01:09:33,505
不幸的是，
Unfortunately,

1103
01:09:33,540 --> 01:09:37,548
今晚来找我的不是天使，
it wasn't an angel that
came to me in the night,

1104
01:09:37,583 --> 01:09:39,548
而是肚子急了。糟透了。
it was the trots. Bad.

1105
01:09:42,592 --> 01:09:45,572
我们现在离伯利恒只有20英里，
We were now just 20
miles from Bethlehem,

1106
01:09:45,607 --> 01:09:47,533
而且这一路走来真是惊心动魄
and what a journey we'd had

1107
01:09:47,568 --> 01:09:51,528
穿越这片已有七千年历史的地区
through a region that's
made history for 7,000 years

1108
01:09:51,563 --> 01:09:54,580
至今仍是头条新闻。
and continues to make
front-page news today.

1109
01:09:56,532 --> 01:10:00,520
不像原来的贤士们，我们得走大绕路
Unlike the original wise men,
we'd had to take huge detours

1110
01:10:00,555 --> 01:10:04,576
要绕开政治地雷，也有真地雷。
around the political
minefields, and the real ones.

1111
01:10:04,611 --> 01:10:06,545
但不知怎么的，我们还是到达了，
And yet somehow we'd made it,

1112
01:10:06,580 --> 01:10:10,564
而且还是开着根本不适合这种路况的车。
in cars that really weren't
built for this kind of work.

1113
01:10:13,560 --> 01:10:15,541
肯定有人会想，
There must have been
people who thought,

1114
01:10:15,576 --> 01:10:19,568
他们是疯子，竟然开跑车横跨中东和沙漠，但我们居然跑到终点，我还在一辆跑车里。
they're idiots setting out across
the Middle East and its deserts

1115
01:10:19,603 --> 01:10:23,560
我真想不到还有什么车比这更适合这趟旅行
in sports cars, but here we are
at the end and I'm still in one.

1116
01:10:25,556 --> 01:10:28,544
比一辆小敞篷跑车更好，
I can't think of anything I'd
rather have done this journey in

1117
01:10:28,579 --> 01:10:31,525
因为这种车能给你，
than a small open-top sports car,

1118
01:10:31,560 --> 01:10:34,508
花不了多少钱，
because what cars
like this give you,

1119
01:10:34,543 --> 01:10:36,473
就是93万英里的蓝天。
for a relatively small outlay,

1120
01:10:36,508 --> 01:10:41,584
is access to 93 million
miles of blue sky.
is access to 93 million
miles of blue sky.

1121
01:10:43,536 --> 01:10:45,493
这种东西根本不敢标价。
You can't really put
a price on that.

1122
01:10:45,528 --> 01:10:49,524
这小小的菲亚特啊，坦白说，成了这趟旅程的惊喜。
This little Fiat has been, it's fair
to say, the surprise of the trip,

1123
01:10:49,559 --> 01:10:53,520
因为没人想到它能跑完。拜托，一辆小小的意大利跑车？
because nobody expected it to finish.
Come on, a small Italian sports car?

1124
01:10:53,555 --> 01:10:54,545
这路上也不是没出岔子。
There have been problems.

1125
01:10:54,580 --> 01:10:57,592
屁股竟然掉了一截。是杰里米干的。
One of its buttocks fell off.
Jeremy did that.

1126
01:10:57,627 --> 01:11:00,481
散热器也给掉了。是我干的。
The radiator fell off. I did that.

1127
01:11:00,516 --> 01:11:03,516
这儿还有股刺鼻的味儿，绝对是我搞的。
And there's a terrible smell
in here, I definitely did that.

1128
01:11:03,551 --> 01:11:05,505
但它硬是熬了过去。
But it's survived them.

1129
01:11:05,540 --> 01:11:08,548
它还在这儿，还让我忍不住笑出声。
It's still here and it's
still making me grin.

1130
01:11:09,596 --> 01:11:11,528
谢啦，小家伙。
Thank you, little mate.

1131
01:11:12,532 --> 01:11:14,540
好，这就到这里，耶路撒冷。
Well, this is it, Jerusalem.

1132
01:11:15,564 --> 01:11:17,513
现在再也不可能出岔子了。
Nothing can go wrong now.

1133
01:11:17,548 --> 01:11:19,596
准备超车啦。
Overtaking manoeuvre coming up.

1134
01:11:21,508 --> 01:11:24,032
冲刺！
SMASHING

1135
01:11:24,067 --> 01:11:26,521
咣——
GUFFAWS

1136
01:11:26,556 --> 01:11:29,520
我的哈勃管！哎哟，哔——！
My Hubble pipe! Oh BEEP!

1137
01:11:32,560 --> 01:11:34,549
在詹姆斯再添点破坏之前，
Before James could
do any more damage,

1138
01:11:34,584 --> 01:11:38,090
我们在橄榄山的停车场把车拽了出来
we pulled over in a car
park on the Mount of Olives

1139
01:11:38,125 --> 01:11:41,596
好决定到底哪辆车更牛逼。
so we could decide which
of our cars was the best.

1140
01:11:43,576 --> 01:11:46,516
我想先来抛砖引玉。
I would like to
speak first on this.

1141
01:11:46,551 --> 01:11:47,553
这玩意儿烂透了。啥？
It's rubbish. What?

1142
01:11:47,588 --> 01:11:51,072
抱歉，地狱里已经给它预留了位置
I'm sorry, there's a
place reserved in Hell

1143
01:11:51,107 --> 01:11:54,521
给那位把变速箱装进车里的家伙。
for the man who put that
gearbox in that car.

1144
01:11:54,556 --> 01:11:58,572
还有那个传动比，叫得响亮的多，真正被选中的少。
And it's the ratios. It's a case of
many are called, but few are chosen

1145
01:11:58,607 --> 01:12:01,481
先手往往沦为第四名，
and many who are first
shall be fourth,

1146
01:12:01,516 --> 01:12:04,536
而排第三的往往还能冲进第二。
and many who are third will
actually kick down into second.

1147
01:12:04,571 --> 01:12:05,525
没戏了！
It's hopeless!

1148
01:12:05,560 --> 01:12:08,584
那我直接问，你们俩想选哪一辆？
So, can I just ask, which of our
two would you choose to have?

1149
01:12:08,619 --> 01:12:11,592
哪一辆让你们看得最渴望？
Which have you looked
at most covetously?

1150
01:12:11,627 --> 01:12:14,532
我羡慕邻居的菲亚特。
I covet my neighbour's Fiat.

1151
01:12:14,567 --> 01:12:16,465
哈哈！真的？好兄弟。
Hee! Really? Good man.

1152
01:12:16,500 --> 01:12:17,549
这倒是挺有意思的，
Now, that's very interesting,

1153
01:12:17,584 --> 01:12:21,536
因为在三辆车里，我会选菲亚特。
because the car of the three
that I would choose is the Fiat.

1154
01:12:21,571 --> 01:12:23,541
呃？我可不拐弯抹角。
Eh? I make no bones about it.

1155
01:12:23,576 --> 01:12:26,508
我依旧认为这是一辆超棒的小车。
I still maintain this is
a fantastic little car.

1156
01:12:26,543 --> 01:12:28,504
我们都喜欢马自达MX-5。真是好车。
We all like the Mazda MX-5.
Great car.

1157
01:12:28,539 --> 01:12:29,521
我跟它没啥感情。
I haven't bonded with it.

1158
01:12:29,556 --> 01:12:34,556
方向盘手感不错，乘坐舒适，但就是不敢爱上它。
The steering is lovely, ride's lovely, but
the one thing you don't do is love it.

1159
01:12:34,591 --> 01:12:37,485
我从没站起来想，‘希望它能行啊！’
I never got up and thought,
I hope it's all right!

1160
01:12:37,520 --> 01:12:40,568
所以，这趟旅程结束后，你们依旧把它当机器看待。就像一台笔记本。
So, at the end of this trip this is
still a machine to you. A laptop.

1161
01:12:40,603 --> 01:12:44,557
所以，大家都同意，意大利车最可靠。
So, we're all agreed, and the
Italian car is the most reliable.

1162
01:12:44,592 --> 01:12:48,556
是啊。不过我们得把这些想法统统甩掉。
Yes. But we have got to get all
these thoughts out of our heads now.

1163
01:12:48,591 --> 01:12:50,501
我们得把节目搞完。
We must complete the programme.

1164
01:12:50,536 --> 01:12:53,556
汽车迷们，先别开车。我们必须把这趟旅程完成。
Car enthusiasts, turn off now.
We've just got to finish this journey.

1165
01:12:53,591 --> 01:12:56,548
我们得完成任务。必须的。
We must complete the
mission. We must.

1166
01:13:04,552 --> 01:13:07,533
不久我们就抵达了伯利恒，
Soon we arrived in Bethlehem,

1167
01:13:07,568 --> 01:13:10,592
感觉真好，站在地球上和平之源
and it felt good to be at
the font of peace on earth

1168
01:13:10,627 --> 01:13:14,512
以及对所有人的善意。
and goodwill to all men.

1169
01:13:30,536 --> 01:13:35,572
天色暗下来时，我们在夜空中看到一道神秘的光
As darkness descended, we saw a
mysterious light in the night sky

1170
01:13:35,607 --> 01:13:37,588
于是决定跟过去。
and decided to follow it.

1171
01:13:47,592 --> 01:13:50,532
这儿肯定是目的地。
This must be the place.

1172
01:13:53,584 --> 01:13:56,493
所以，我们到了，
So, here we are,

1173
01:13:56,528 --> 01:14:01,536
一道天光射下来，意味着我们的探险要收场了。
a shaft of heavenly light indicating
that our quest is at an end.

1174
01:14:09,584 --> 01:14:11,572
就是这里。
This is it.

1175
01:14:18,560 --> 01:14:20,536
有牧羊人的痕迹。
Evidence of shepherds.

1176
01:14:47,580 --> 01:14:50,512
我说过有老鼠的。嘘。
I told you there was a mouse. Shh.

1177
01:14:55,516 --> 01:15:01,028
我们是三位智者，远道而来，携带礼物。
We're three wise men and we have
travelled far from the East with gifts.

1178
01:15:01,063 --> 01:15:06,540
黄金、洗发水——这有点失策——还有个电子玩具。
Gold, shampoo - that was a bit of
a mistake - and an electronic toy.

1179
01:15:10,576 --> 01:15:13,596
让我们看看这位降临的孩子。
Let us see this child who
has been born unto us.

1180
01:15:13,631 --> 01:15:15,536
好啊，给我们看看。好啊。
Yes, let us. Yes.

1181
01:15:17,556 --> 01:15:18,564
倒抽一口气
GASPS

1182
01:15:19,564 --> 01:15:22,564
激昂的音乐
DRAMATIC MUSIC

1183
01:15:27,588 --> 01:15:29,580
我没想到会这样。
I wasn't expecting that.

1184
01:15:36,512 --> 01:15:38,520
就在这炸裂的瞬间，
And on that bombshell,

1185
01:15:38,555 --> 01:15:40,493
该收尾了。
it is time to end.

1186
01:15:40,528 --> 01:15:42,596
非常感谢观看，晚安。
Thank you so much for
watching, goodnight.

1187
01:15:42,631 --> 01:15:45,540
♪ 一束希望
♪ A ray of hope

1188
01:15:46,536 --> 01:15:49,580
♪ 在天空中闪烁
♪ Flickers in the sky

1189
01:15:50,576 --> 01:15:53,560
♪ 一颗小星星
♪ A tiny star

1190
01:15:54,524 --> 01:15:58,508
♪ 在高空点亮
♪ Lights up way up high

1191
01:15:59,540 --> 01:16:02,542
♪ 照亮整个大地
♪ All across the land

1192
01:16:02,577 --> 01:16:06,052
♪ 迎来全新的黎明
♪ Dawns a brand-new morn

1193
01:16:06,087 --> 01:16:09,528
♪ 事已至此……
♪ This comes to pass...

